# Majo Runtime example

If you downloaded the example ZIP, extract it into an empty directory. Install Godot 4.7.2 .NET and the .NET 8 SDK. Run `dotnet build Example.csproj` from the project directory, then open `project.godot` and let the editor finish importing. Press F5 to run. Click or press Space to advance and click a choice to continue.

Follow the [first scene tutorial (Chinese)](addons/majo_runtime/Docs/first-scene.zh-CN.md) to replace the sample dialogue and add your own background image, character sprite, and music.

Both addons and their licenses are included. The sample story and host code are covered by `addons/majo_runtime/LICENSE`. See the [addon guide](addons/majo_runtime/README.md) for checked exports and validated platforms.

Projects generated by `init` already have `majo.lock.json`. If you started with an example ZIP and want to manage addon upgrades, download the matching `with-yarn` addon ZIP and `SHA256SUMS` from the same release. Run the manager from this project directory.

```sh
python3 addons/majo_runtime/Tools/majo.py install --project . --archive "/path/to/majo-runtime-VERSION-with-yarn.zip" --sha256 EXPECTED_SHA256
```

Use the path to your matching bundled addon ZIP and its checksum from `SHA256SUMS`. See the [managed upgrade guide](addons/majo_runtime/README.md#install-a-published-candidate) for switching versions and rolling back.
